                        <field name="dc_description">At foot of title: "For the best essay on which subject a prize of £10 was offered by the Right Honorable the Baroness Burdett Coutts. Prize not awarded to any of the essays, none being sufficiently practical. The accompanying two essays, out of those received on the subject of killing fish wite [sic] the least cruelty, have been published by the directions, and at the expense of the Right Hon. the Baroness Burdett Coutts [...]". -- Copies to be had free, on application to Thomas F. Brady, 11, Percy-Place, Dublin. -- Includes introduction, signed "Kosciusko, March 26th, 1874". -- Second essay includes preface "To the reader" signed "H. R., 41 Lower Sackville-Street, Dublin". -- Second essay includes 3 fold-out leaves with illustrations (2 in colour). -- Includes notes. -- Includes, at end of volume, table of contents and list of illustrations for second essay. </field>
